## 4. MT.1223's risk list has no anchor to the published permission set

`Get-MtEntraAgentHighRiskGraphPermissionFinding` hardcodes 11 high-risk Graph permissions with an attack-path classification. The selection is deliberate — `RoleManagement.ReadWrite.Directory` is blocked for agents, so the closely-related `RoleAssignmentSchedule.ReadWrite.Directory`, which is not blocked, is used instead.

Nothing ties the list to Microsoft's published blocked-for-agents list though, so as permissions move between categories the check silently drifts: a newly blocked permission becomes dead weight, and a newly unblocked escalation path is missed. Worth deciding whether this wants a refresh path (as `build/Update-MtEamClassification.ps1` does for the EAM tiers) or just a documented review cadence.

## 5. Minor: MT.1210 overlaps a platform constraint
